{"text": "19\n\nPME RESEARCH LABORATORY, December 1976/January 1977\n\n26.\n\nSpecial Analytical Services\n\nDetermination of N-Nitrosamines in Tobacco\n\nWork was continued with the preparation of volatile\nN-nitroso compounds of easily nitrosatable substances\nsuch as secondary amines, present in tobacco in a high\nconcentration.\n\nResults\n\nN-Nitrosodimethylamine (bp. 145-146\u00b0/720 mm), N-nitro-\nsodiethylamine (bp. 168\u00b0/715 mm), N-nitrosodipropylamine\n(op. 889/12 mm), N-nitrosodiisopropylamine (bp. 101-1040/\n15 mm), 1-nitrosopyrrolidine (bp. 97-100\u00b0/15 mm) and 1-\nnitrosopiperidine (115-119\u00b0/12 mn) were prepared in high\nyield (70-85%) by treating the corresponding secondary\namines (or amine hydrochlorides) with sodium nitrite in\ndiluted hydrochloric acid solutions according to\n\nR2NH + NaNOz + HCL \u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014 __RN-NO + NaCl + H20.\n\n\u2018The nitroso compounds, stable, viscous oils, were purified\nby distillation. The preparation of dibutyl-, diisobuty1-,\ndipentyl- and dihexyl-nitrosamines as well as of N-nitroso-\nmethylaniline and of N-nitroso-ethylaniline is in progress.\n\nIn addition to N-nitrosamine preparations we are currently\nexamining i) methods for the direct and quantitative deter-\nmination of underivatized N-nitrosamines by g.1.c., ii)\npossible routes for the separation of N-nitrosamines from\ntobacco and iii) clean-up procedures.\n\nTobacco Alkaloid Analyses\n\nEight ground tobacco samples (submitted by \"Landesanstalt,\nForchheim\") of the joint experiment on tobacco alkaloid\ndetermination by g.l.c., which was agreed on by \"TFA\" on\nMay 5, 1976, have been investigated.\n\n\u00a3o9stoszoz",
